WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:02.316
- I was shot about 16 years ago,

00:00:02.316 --> 00:00:06.937
and I still feel the effects from that day

00:00:06.937 --> 00:00:09.596
in every aspect of my life.

00:00:09.596 --> 00:00:14.596
(slow, dramatic music)

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.647
I was working as a camp
counselor when I was

00:00:21.647 --> 00:00:24.487
16 years old at the North
Valley Jewish Community Center.

00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:26.268
One day, after playing capture the flag,

00:00:26.268 --> 00:00:29.144
I was walking in with one
of my favorite campers.

00:00:29.144 --> 00:00:30.781
We decided to walk to the
front of the building,

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:32.685
because that's where the
rest of my campers were,

00:00:32.685 --> 00:00:34.241
who were all five and six-year-old kids,

00:00:34.241 --> 00:00:36.648
and as we walked to the
front of the building,

00:00:36.648 --> 00:00:37.780
a man walked in

00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:42.069
carrying a semi-automatic uzi replica gun,

00:00:42.069 --> 00:00:43.369
and started shooting,

00:00:43.369 --> 00:00:46.051
and he shot off about
70 rounds of ammunition

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:47.570
into the building.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.899
He shot me first, and then
he just started spraying.

00:00:53.481 --> 00:00:54.503
He showed up on a day when there were

00:00:54.503 --> 00:00:55.618
a lot of children there,

00:00:55.618 --> 00:00:58.416
about 350 kids at the
Jewish Community Center.

00:00:58.416 --> 00:01:01.575
And so I grabbed James
and I ran into a classroom

00:01:01.575 --> 00:01:02.735
that was right in front of us,

00:01:02.735 --> 00:01:03.942
and there were a bunch of little kids,

00:01:03.942 --> 00:01:05.556
five and six-years-old in that room

00:01:05.556 --> 00:01:08.517
with my co-counselors, and
I was covered in blood,

00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:11.233
and we still heard shooting outside.

00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:12.418
Bang, bang, bang.

00:01:12.418 --> 00:01:14.600
The campers all looked
up at me and kept saying,

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.603
'What's all over Mindy,
what's all over Mindy?'

00:01:16.603 --> 00:01:17.700
There happened to be an emergency exit

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.301
in that one room that we went into.

00:01:20.301 --> 00:01:21.066
We ran outside.

00:01:21.066 --> 00:01:23.145
There was a glass sliding door behind us,

00:01:23.145 --> 00:01:25.839
and he saw us running and
shot through the glass door,

00:01:25.839 --> 00:01:27.545
and the glass exploded behind us.

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:29.147
I had lost a lot of blood at that point,

00:01:29.147 --> 00:01:30.877
and couldn't continue running,

00:01:30.877 --> 00:01:33.187
so we closed our eyes and played dead

00:01:33.187 --> 00:01:34.662
until we heard sirens.

00:01:34.662 --> 00:01:38.778
(sirens)

00:01:40.107 --> 00:01:42.812
And to this day, I still
have quite a bit of shrapnel

00:01:42.812 --> 00:01:44.508
inside my leg,

00:01:44.508 --> 00:01:47.468
and it's a constant reminder
of what I went through.

00:01:47.468 --> 00:01:49.279
The thing that I remember most is

00:01:49.279 --> 00:01:53.260
when you breathe in, you
feel air inside your lungs,

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.980
but you've never felt air anywhere else

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.720
inside your body, and immediately after

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.042
the bullets passed through me,

00:02:00.042 --> 00:02:02.201
I remember feeling invisible,

00:02:02.201 --> 00:02:04.940
because there was air running through me

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.206
that I had never felt before,

00:02:06.206 --> 00:02:08.203
and that's the instant that I knew

00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:12.348
something, a, wasn't
right, b, I had been shot,

00:02:12.348 --> 00:02:15.471
and the moment where I
started thinking about death.

00:02:15.471 --> 00:02:19.163
He shot three five-year-old kids,

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:21.868
myself, who was 16 at the time,

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:24.022
and a 65-year-old woman
who was the receptionist.

00:02:24.022 --> 00:02:26.715
The ones that weren't shot,

00:02:26.715 --> 00:02:29.078
they are, you know, in their 20s now,

00:02:29.078 --> 00:02:31.737
and are continuing to have
horrific nightmares about

00:02:31.737 --> 00:02:33.455
this bad man with a gun, coming in,

00:02:33.455 --> 00:02:35.033
trying to take their lives away.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:39.591
(slow, sad music)

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.836
A year later, I tried
to go away to college,

00:02:42.836 --> 00:02:44.239
and I had a complete breakdown

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:46.074
within the first six days of being there.

00:02:46.074 --> 00:02:48.281
A kid walked down the
hall with a Nerf gun,

00:02:48.281 --> 00:02:50.440
and he was just, you know,
having fun, laughing,

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.832
and shooting everybody with Nerf balls,

00:02:52.832 --> 00:02:56.442
and the second the Nerf
ball hit me, I broke down.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.902
They put me in a psych ward of a hospital,

00:02:59.902 --> 00:03:01.515
and I felt crazy.

00:03:01.515 --> 00:03:04.170
So, I typically have a
panic attack every time

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.301
I see a mass shooting.

00:03:05.301 --> 00:03:08.099
Virginia Tech, immediately
after I had a panic attack.

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:10.642
Sandy Hook, instantly panic attack.

00:03:10.642 --> 00:03:13.323
And I know, moving
forward, I will continue

00:03:13.323 --> 00:03:15.785
to have the reactions like I do.

00:03:15.785 --> 00:03:18.362
What scares me is not having the reaction.

00:03:18.362 --> 00:03:20.963
It scares me when we become numb.

00:03:20.963 --> 00:03:22.622
People always tell me that
I was in the wrong place

00:03:22.622 --> 00:03:25.084
at the wrong time, but, in reality,

00:03:25.084 --> 00:03:26.884
I was in the right
place at the right time.

00:03:26.884 --> 00:03:30.506
I was 16, you know, I was
working with my little kids,

00:03:30.506 --> 00:03:33.606
I was protecting my kids

00:03:33.606 --> 00:03:35.290
and our future as a society,

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.635
and so how dare you tell
me I was in the wrong place

00:03:37.635 --> 00:03:38.633
at the wrong time.

00:03:38.633 --> 00:03:40.491
He was in the wrong
place at the wrong time.

00:03:43.141 --> 00:03:44.775
I think it happened to me for a reason.

00:03:44.775 --> 00:03:46.098
I don't think there are a lot of people

00:03:46.998 --> 00:03:49.557
that could've handled what happened to me

00:03:49.557 --> 00:03:51.182
as well as I have.

00:03:51.182 --> 00:03:53.539
I have definitely suffered emotionally,

00:03:53.539 --> 00:03:54.723
I continue to suffer.

00:03:54.723 --> 00:03:57.835
I'm 33, I'm married, I own a home,

00:03:57.835 --> 00:04:00.842
I live in a wonderful, wonderful city,

00:04:00.842 --> 00:04:03.575
and I couldn't be happier,

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:05.869
and had I not been shot,

00:04:05.869 --> 00:04:07.889
all of those things probably
wouldn't necessarily

00:04:07.889 --> 00:04:09.073
have happened to me.

00:04:09.073 --> 00:04:11.012
But, yeah, I would take it away.

00:04:11.012 --> 00:04:12.591
I don't put this on anybody.

00:04:12.591 --> 00:04:14.402
But if it could've happened to anybody,

00:04:14.402 --> 00:04:15.668
I am glad it happened to me,

00:04:15.668 --> 00:04:18.408
because nobody deserves to
go through that kind of pain.

00:04:18.408 --> 00:04:23.174
(slow, dramatic music)

